Package: sparcproteomics
Type: Package
Title: Engine-Agnostic Downstream Analysis of Quantitative Proteomics Data
Version: 0.2.0
URL: https://github.com/arunkumaran07/SPARC_proteomics
BugReports: https://github.com/arunkumaran07/SPARC_proteomics/issues
Authors@R:
    person("arunkumaran07", email = "arunkumaran07@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Downstream analysis of quantitative proteomics data from
    DIA-NN, Spectronaut, MaxQuant, DIA-NN precursor reports, peptide tables
    or a generic matrix. A YAML
    configuration (or an interactive wizard) declares the species, sample
    groups, control group, comparisons, imputation method and statistical
    method. Data are held in a 'SummarizedExperiment'. Differential abundance
    is tested with 'limma' moderated statistics or Welch/Student t-tests on
    the un-imputed matrix, with optional Reactome enrichment and optional
    large-language-model interpretation through the Anthropic API.
